invariant: INV-17
file: sha256_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: compress_blocks returns without wiping its block_state, so its dead
  frame keeps the last block's message schedule and the state before and
  after it. Under HMAC the first block is the key, and the state after it
  stands for the key: whoever reads it computes any MAC under that key.
  Every digest is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test
  copies the stack below each kind of call and looks for four schedule,
  message or state words in a row. The wipe sits outside the two
  architecture arms, so the x86-64 build the script runs under
  qemu-x86_64 holds it for arm64 too. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    run_blocks(&c, h, p, blocks);
    ct_wipe(&c, sizeof c);
--- new
    run_blocks(&c, h, p, blocks);
